## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Tư: Quyết định thiết kế

> *"Today I attacked my own API with a load generator, and the interesting part is what killed it.*
> *Normal traffic was fine. But twenty concurrent requests against the login endpoint took the whole thing down. The reason is argon2 — it's deliberately slow and deliberately memory-hungry, about a hundred milliseconds and nineteen megabytes per attempt. That's exactly what you want against offline password cracking. It's also a denial of service vector, because it's expensive work an unauthenticated stranger can ask me to do.*
> *So login is rate limited to five attempts per fifteen minutes per IP — much tighter than everything else, which is a hundred per minute per user.*
> *One detail I want to call out: login is limited by IP and everything else by user ID. On the login endpoint I don't know who they are yet — that's the thing they're trying to establish.*
> *The counters live in Redis, not in process memory, because I run more than one instance. An in-memory counter would give an attacker double the allowance.*
> *And to be honest about the limit: this stops one attacker and it stops a user hammering a button. It does not stop a distributed attack from a thousand IPs. That needs something in front of my server, which I don't have."*

Đoạn cuối — thừa nhận ranh giới — là đoạn tăng độ tin cậy nhiều nhất.

**5 từ mới:**

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `memory-hungry` | ngốn bộ nhớ | *It's deliberately memory-hungry.* |
| `denial of service vector` | đường tấn công từ chối dịch vụ | *It's also a DoS vector.* |
| `call out` (v) | nêu bật ra | *One detail I want to call out.* |
| `allowance` | hạn mức được cấp | *That gives an attacker double the allowance.* |
| `hammer a button` | bấm nút liên tục | *It stops a user hammering a button.* |

